Hi list,

I would like to plot several x (continuous) vs. different y's
(continuous), a bit like plot(dataset) in base R, but for one variable
at a time. I was wondering if there is any way of doing that in only one
 ggplot call? I'm using melt and fact_grid to plot relations with
factors, but I can't figure how it could be done with molten data in the
 case here (if it could be done at all).

Any idea would be appreciated.

I've made a dummy dataset, as far.

dummy = data.frame(x=rnorm(20),y1=rnorm(20),y2=rnorm(20),y3=rnorm(20))

Thank you!

guillaume

