Manual,

I've been trying, but I'm not sure it's working.

I wondering if maybe it would be better to melt the dataframe and color with scale_colour_manual().

molten.aves<-melt(aves, id.vars=c("x", "y", "sitio"))

ggplot(data=molten.aves, aes(x=x, y=y))+geom_point(aes(colour=variable, size=value))+geom_text(aes(x=x+500, label=sitio), size=2, hjust=0, alpha=0.5)+theme_bw()+scale_colour_manual(values=c("pink", "black"))

Better? Worse?

Brandon

